# Claude Code permissions that must exist on EVERY machine.
#
# One `permissions.allow` entry per line. Blank lines and `#` comments ignored.
# `bin/ai-claude-permissions` merges these into the USER-level settings file
# (~/.claude/settings.json), so they cover every project on the machine.
#
# This file is additive: the script never removes an entry a machine already
# has, and never touches `ask` or anything else in the file. Delete a line here
# and it simply stops being enforced on the next sync; machines that already
# have it keep it. The one exception is a `retire:` line, which names an entry
# this file once installed and removes exactly that entry (`retire:deny:...`
# for a deny entry) wherever it is still present.
#
# Browser page-inspection tools. A session doing visual/UI verification needs
# these to screenshot and read a rendered page; without them it stops on a
# permission prompt that nobody is sitting there to answer. Added 2026-08-13.
mcp__playwright__browser_evaluate
mcp__claude-in-chrome__javascript_tool

# Read-only commands that 245 sessions in 2026-09/10 stopped on (transcript
# analysis 2026-10-21). Read-only prefixes only. Deliberately NOT here: `find`
# (it has -delete/-exec) and `timeout` (a prefix rule would allow any command
# behind it).
Bash(git status:*)
Bash(git log:*)
Bash(git diff:*)
Bash(git branch --show-current:*)
Bash(git branch -a:*)
Bash(git branch --list:*)
Bash(git show:*)
Bash(gh pr view:*)
Bash(gh pr checks:*)
Bash(gh issue view:*)
Bash(ls:*)
Bash(cat:*)
Bash(grep:*)
Bash(rg:*)
Bash(wc:*)
Bash(head:*)
Bash(tail:*)

# `gh run watch` is refused; wait with a background `ai-pr-wait` instead. A lone
# `sleep` is legitimate and is NOT denied: hand-written sleep-in-a-loop shapes are
# refused by the tested pr-poll-guard hook, which is the contract. The broad
# `deny:Bash(sleep:*)` shipped on 2026-10-21 (PR #1932) is retired below so every
# machine that installed it loses it on the next sync (#1962).
deny:Bash(gh run watch:*)
retire:deny:Bash(sleep:*)

# Read-only commands from a scan of the 50 most recent transcripts on edge-dev3
# (2026-10-21) that Claude Code does not already auto-allow. Excluded on purpose:
# `gcloud secrets` (prints secret values), `ai-task-gates start/check` (they
# record gate state), `gcloud builds retry/triggers` (can change builds).
Bash(ai-pr-wait *)
Bash(bin/ai-pr-wait *)
Bash(ai-doc-safety)
Bash(ai-doc-safety *)
Bash(bin/ai-doc-safety)
Bash(bin/ai-doc-safety *)
Bash(ai-review doctor)
Bash(gcloud builds list *)
Bash(gcloud builds describe *)
Bash(gcloud builds log *)
Bash(gcloud run services list *)
Bash(gcloud run services describe *)
Bash(gcloud logging read *)
